<div class="field-unit__label">
  <%= f.label field.attribute, 'Limits' %>
</div>
<div class="field-unit__field">
  <%#
    The blast radius of an entitlement edit, shown where the edit happens (docs/p11/03-plans-entitlements.md).
    P-FINAL made the rule the server's rather than this paragraph's: while a plan has billed subscribers it can
    be widened but not narrowed (BillingPlan#refuse_narrowing_while_billed), so the copy now says what will
    happen rather than asking the operator to be careful.
  %>
  <% billed = field.resource.persisted? ? field.resource.subscriptions.where(status: BillingSubscription::BILLED_STATUSES).count : 0 %>
  <% if billed.positive? %>
    <p class="mb-3 text-[0.8125rem] text-y-800">
      <strong><%= billed %></strong> account<%= 's' unless billed == 1 %> currently pay for this plan. Widening it —
      adding a feature, raising or clearing a ceiling, selling another channel — applies to all of them immediately.
      Narrowing it is refused: to sell something smaller, create a new plan and move those accounts to it, or grant a
      per-account override for a single exception. Either way the change is recorded in the audit log.
    </p>
  <% end %>
  <% BillingPlan::LIMIT_KEYS.each do |key| %>
    <div class="mb-2">
      <label for="billing_plan_limits_<%= key %>"><%= field.label(key) %></label>
      <input type="number" min="0" step="1"
             id="billing_plan_limits_<%= key %>"
             name="<%= f.object_name %>[<%= field.attribute %>][<%= key %>]"
             value="<%= field.limits[key] %>"
             placeholder="Unlimited">
    </div>
  <% end %>
  <p class="text-xs text-n-slate-11">Leave empty for unlimited. 0 = not allowed.</p>
  <p class="text-xs text-n-slate-11">Commerce stores: stores an account keeps connected (any platform; disconnected stores do not count). Applies when the plan includes Lynomia Commerce.</p>
</div>
